.SH NAME
robne-recommend - Compute recommendations from ROS CSV or stored digests


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrobne recommend [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Compute recommendations from ROS CSV or stored digests.

.PP
JSON envelope "version" is per-run (max plugin sibling this invocation, or 10
when business hours is on). It does not identify this binary. Run robne version
for binary identity and the plugin → envelope capability table.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--apply-schema\fP[=false]
	bootstrap or upgrade embedded migrations on a dedicated database

.PP
\fB--config\fP=""
	YAML overlay (skips ./robne.yaml; still overlays the user file)

.PP
\fB--format\fP="json"
	stdout format: json, csv, or table

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for recommend

.PP
\fB--input\fP=""
	directory, .csv, .tar.gz, or postgres:// URL (recompute from stored digests)

.PP
\fB--no-user-config\fP[=false]
	skip user YAML/JSON (same as ROBNE_NO_USER_CONFIG=1)

.PP
\fB--now\fP=""
	RFC3339 decay/staleness clock (does not slide term windows; default is max interval_end)

.PP
\fB--output\fP=""
	postgres:// or postgresql:// URL for a CLI-owned database (use case c)

.PP
\fB--pg-url-file\fP=""
	file containing a postgres URL (password off argv)

.PP
\fB--plugins\fP=""
	comma-separated allowlist (default: all shipped plugins; omit to skip missing inputs)

.PP
\fB--rate-card\fP=""
	rate-card JSON overlay (skips ./rate-card.json)


